From 362675b75d0617a33c451707ae03e3c69aafbca0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 04:16:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08026/11362] The dedup-key verifier was writing its output
 into scripts/

A post-commit smoke run of the newly-committed harness left an untracked
`scripts/xgame_dedup_cap3000.json` behind. The script resolved its output
directory as "next to this file", which was right while it lived in a scratch
directory and became wrong the moment it moved into `scripts/`: every run dropped
a JSON blob into a tracked source directory, where the next `git add -A` would
have committed it as stray output.

Output now goes to `$XG_OUT_DIR` if set, else the CURRENT working directory --
deliberately never beside the source. `REPO` is derived from the file's own
location (honouring `$CARNOT_REPO_ROOT`) instead of a hardcoded absolute path, so
the harness works in a worktree or a different checkout. The engine store now
defaults to a temp directory rather than a path under the script, because
`results/arc_e3` is tracked read-only evidence and an induction triggered from
here must never be able to reach it.

Verified by running the committed script from an unrelated cwd: the artifact lands
there, `scripts/` stays clean, and the partition verdict is unchanged
(`all_landed_state_key_partitions_identical: true`).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
